# Tree
arena (aliases: ar) [test.command.arena, OP]
  create [test.command.arena.create, ALL]
    --force, -f
    <name: StringArgument> [size: IntegerArgument] [test.command.arena.create.name.size, ALL]
  delete [test.command.arena.delete, OP]
    <name: StringArgument> [test.command.arena.delete.name, OP]
  invite [test.command.arena.invite, OP]
    <arena: StringArgument> <players...: PlayerArgument> [test.command.arena.invite.arena.players, OP]
  join [test.command.arena.join, OP]
    <arena: StringArgument> [player: PlayerArgument] [test.command.arena.join.arena.player, OP]
  list [test.command.arena.list, OP]
    --limit, -n <limit>
  stats [test.command.arena.stats, OP]
    <arena: StringArgument> [test.command.arena.stats.arena, OP]

# Permissions
| Permission | Default | Route | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `test.command.arena` | `OP` | `/arena` |  |
| `test.command.arena.create` | `ALL` | `/arena create` | Create arenas |
| `test.command.arena.create.name.size` | `ALL` | `/arena create <name> [size]` |  |
| `test.command.arena.delete` | `OP` | `/arena delete` |  |
| `test.command.arena.delete.name` | `OP` | `/arena delete <name>` |  |
| `test.command.arena.invite` | `OP` | `/arena invite` |  |
| `test.command.arena.invite.arena.players` | `OP` | `/arena invite <arena> <players...>` |  |
| `test.command.arena.join` | `OP` | `/arena join` |  |
| `test.command.arena.join.arena.player` | `OP` | `/arena join <arena> [player]` |  |
| `test.command.arena.list` | `OP` | `/arena list` |  |
| `test.command.arena.stats` | `OP` | `/arena stats` |  |
| `test.command.arena.stats.arena` | `OP` | `/arena stats <arena>` |  |

# Suggestions of /arena delete
help, lobby
# Admin
/arena -> 1
    --------------------------------------------------
    Manage arenas
    Usage:
      /arena create: Create an arena
      /arena delete
      /arena invite
      /arena join
      /arena list
      /arena stats
    --------------------------------------------------
/arena create -> 1
    --------------------------------------------------
    Create an arena
    Usage:
      /arena create [options] <name> [size]
    
    Options:
      -f, --force: Replace an existing arena
    --------------------------------------------------
/arena create lobby2 -> 1
    Created lobby2 with 16 slots
/arena create -f big 32 -> 1
    Created big with 32 slots (forced)
/arena create huge 100 -> RuntimeException: Command syntax error: Integer must not be more than 64, found 100 at position 18: ...eate huge <--[HERE]
    
